WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:10.049
Why is Donald Trump so interested in punishing
the Islamic Republic of Iran?

00:00:10.049 --> 00:00:13.910
If you’ve seen the previous videos on this
series, you might believe that he’s interested

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:21.940
in raising oil prices, helping his Saudi friends or just showing the European Union who’s

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:24.980
boss.

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:26.430
But here is another hypothesis…

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:31.119
What if what Donald Trump is going after is…
the end of authoritarian rule in Iran?

00:00:31.119 --> 00:00:32.860
This is not a stupid theory.

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:34.920
Iran is at the edge of economic collapse.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:39.130
Anti government protests are frequent and,
unlike other countries in the region, Iran

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:50.030
does have a secular, liberal and democratic
opposition.

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:53.760
This means you don’t need to wage a real
war to bring democracy to this country.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:57.190
Choking the regime financially could be enough.

00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:06.830
If this plan went as well as it sounds, Donald
Trump could even win a Peace Nobel prize.

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:11.330
Obama would look dumb, and Trump would win
the 2020 elections for sure.

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:13.580
But… what if it doesn’t turn out as well
as planned?

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:17.010
Is the Ayatolah regime as weak as we think?

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:20.210
Can Trump win this bet?

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:29.090
We will cover all of this in this video.

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:30.920
Iran is the man America loves to hate.

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:34.920
Of course, the White House claims that the
nuclear sanctions are not meant to topple

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.180
the regime but…

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:43.390
Is that true?

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:48.570
White House national-security adviser John
Bolton says the United States is not seeking

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:53.560
to topple Iran's government, but says Washington
does want authorities in Tehran to change

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:54.670
their behavior.

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:59.549
The truth is, for decades, America has been
trying to do everything possible to curb the

00:01:59.549 --> 00:02:00.549
Ayatolahs’ power.

00:02:00.549 --> 00:02:02.890
For example… have you ever heard of Radio
Free Europe?

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:07.420
During the cold war, the American congress
created this radio to spread anti communist

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:09.410
messages in the Soviet Union.

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:11.009
Today, this radio still exists.

00:02:11.009 --> 00:02:15.890
Actually, they have their offices very close
to where I’m recording this video, in Prague,

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:16.890
Czech Republic.

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:17.890
And guess what!

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:22.650
This radio has a whole department devoted
to Iran.

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:30.040
They broadcast news in the farsi language
to spread anti Ayatola messages inside the

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:33.090
country.

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:38.480
This means Washington is definitely interested
in a regime change in Tehran.

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:42.450
Another matter is whether it’s possible
or not.

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:48.220
And now you might wonder… is Iran really
such a horrible dictatorship?

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:52.790
At the end of the day, they have elections
and political parties, right?

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:55.790
Well, yes and no.

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:59.240
Yes, it is true that Iranians can vote for
their president.

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:06.540
But the actual person in charge is the Supreme
Leader, Ayatolah Khamenei.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:10.460
For a better understanding, Khamenei chooses
most of the ministers and has the ultimate

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:17.610
word on international affairs and many important
laws.

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:23.240
Of course, political dissidents are prosecuted
and often killed by the government.

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:28.569
In fact, despite having some opposition movements…
there are almost no important leaders.

00:03:28.569 --> 00:03:29.569
Why?

00:03:29.569 --> 00:03:33.860
Well, all of them are dead, imprisoned or
exiled.

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:36.890
And what happens with the pro system political
forces?

00:03:36.890 --> 00:03:42.989
Well… rather than political parties, we
should talk about different factions here.

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:47.830
On one hand, we have the so called hard liners.

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:52.440
These are the people that support the system
created by Khomeini to the letter: religious

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:55.860
law and the state led economy.

00:03:55.860 --> 00:04:01.709
Then we have the reformists who want to change
the regime from the inside.

00:04:01.709 --> 00:04:07.209
As you can imagine, this faction has less
and less power nowadays.

00:04:07.209 --> 00:04:13.739
Finally we have the pragmatists, whose most
important representative is the current president:

00:04:13.739 --> 00:04:14.950
HASSAN ROUHANNI.

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:19.359
They are somewhere in between the hard liners
and the reformists.

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:23.710
They want some economic reforms and better
relations with the West, but still want to

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:26.830
keep some religious control in political matters.

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:30.979
And here we have the second question… is
it really possible for this whole political

00:04:30.979 --> 00:04:32.620
system to fall apart?

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:34.949
Well… there is a chance.

00:04:34.949 --> 00:04:39.050
You see, when the economic does OK, it’s
easy to keep an authoritarian system going.

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:43.849
Many citizens are happy to trade freedom for
welfare.

00:04:43.849 --> 00:04:47.580
But Iran has spent too much time without welfare.

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:51.080
Iranian currency, the RIAL, is devaluating
day after day.

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:53.770
And this has led to brutal inflation.

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:58.639
Some non official estimations claim that Iran
will have more than a 100% inflation rate

00:04:58.639 --> 00:04:59.789
this year.

00:04:59.789 --> 00:05:02.520
That means that some prices change on daily
basis.

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:05.370
Many foods like chicken are starting to become
scarce.

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:13.020
And there are more and more people living
below the poverty line.

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:17.089
Even with the government privatizations, the
economy is a mess.

00:05:17.089 --> 00:05:20.270
We already told you here, on VisualPolitik,
at the beginning of the year.

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:24.569
2018 started with massive protests against
the Rouhani government.

00:05:24.569 --> 00:05:28.639
And many of those protesters were young university
students who wanted a shift in the system.

00:05:28.639 --> 00:05:32.119
A shift to one that’s democratic, secular
and liberal.

00:05:32.119 --> 00:05:35.039
But the question, the real question here is…

00:05:35.039 --> 00:05:37.580
Is all of this enough to cause a regime change?

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:44.779
Today we will answer this question but, before
we do, let’s take a look back at history.

00:05:44.779 --> 00:05:47.309
THE PRAETORIAN GUARD

00:05:47.309 --> 00:05:50.729
In the year 1979 the Islamic Revolution started
in Iran.

00:05:50.729 --> 00:05:55.490
The Supreme Leader back then, the Ayatolah
Khomeini knew that the army might betray him

00:05:55.490 --> 00:06:00.180
at any moment.

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:03.229
After decades serving the SHAH of Persia,
it was hard for them to just change their

00:06:03.229 --> 00:06:04.899
loyalties overnight.

00:06:04.899 --> 00:06:08.699
This is why, in order to avoid a coup d’etat,
Khomeini created his own parallel army.

00:06:08.699 --> 00:06:11.759
This is how the Islamic Revolutionary Guard
was created.

00:06:11.759 --> 00:06:17.550
A sort of modern day praetorian guard designed
to ‘preserve the Islamic Republican System’.

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:19.930
In the beginning, all the members were volunteers.

00:06:19.930 --> 00:06:22.849
But things changed in the 80s.

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:27.409
Back then, Iran started a war with Iraq.

00:06:27.409 --> 00:06:29.110
And who did they send to the front?

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:34.539
Of course, they sent these praetorians who
were willing to do anything for their cause.

00:06:34.539 --> 00:06:42.819
And… you know, in times of warfare, there’s
always enough money for more weapons.

00:06:42.819 --> 00:06:48.159
This is how the Islamic Revolutionary Guard
gained more and more influence, more weaponry

00:06:48.159 --> 00:06:49.159
and more experience.

00:06:49.159 --> 00:06:54.150
By the end of the Iran-Iraq war, this praetorian
guard already had more than 130,000 soldiers

00:06:54.150 --> 00:07:01.030
plus many other smaller corps that depended
on them.

00:07:01.030 --> 00:07:08.990
Today, this revolutionary guard has its own
intelligence service, parallel to the government’s

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:10.219
ministry of intelligence.

00:07:10.219 --> 00:07:14.949
And they can imprison or investigate people
without even reporting to the authorities.

00:07:14.949 --> 00:07:19.349
In other words, they are the cornerstone of
the Islamic Revolution but, then again, they

00:07:19.349 --> 00:07:21.819
have a parallel system.

00:07:21.819 --> 00:07:30.300
And why are they so important?

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:33.830
The truth is… as far as the economy goes,
it’s hard to create an alternative to the

00:07:33.830 --> 00:07:38.919
system if you have an elite corp spying on
any would-be political activist.

00:07:38.919 --> 00:07:42.110
And yes, we are talking about an elite corp
here.

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:43.819
Perfectly trained for hybrid warfare.

00:07:43.819 --> 00:07:48.400
They have fought in many other wars such as
Syria, Iraq and even Afghanistan.

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:51.789
And all the experts say their training is
world class.

00:07:51.789 --> 00:07:55.139
And now you might wonder…

00:07:55.139 --> 00:07:58.490
How can they buy weapons?

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:02.669
I mean… if Iran is so isolated from the
international market….

00:08:02.669 --> 00:08:03.830
How is that possible?

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:08.249
Well… the truth is, for decades, Iran has
had its own weapon manufacturing industry.

00:08:08.249 --> 00:08:09.860
Yes, you heard that right.

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:13.659
They use Chinese and Russian designs but the
manufacturing is done in Iran.

00:08:13.659 --> 00:08:17.909
So now of course the question is, won’t
they be affected by these economic sanctions?

00:08:17.909 --> 00:08:22.129
At the end of the day, if Iran has no money,
this Guard won’t be able to buy bullets

00:08:22.129 --> 00:08:23.789
and weapons, right?

00:08:23.789 --> 00:08:31.499
Well, my dear viewers… nothing could be
further from the truth.

00:08:31.499 --> 00:08:41.530
External pressure and lack of foreign competitors
will most likely help the IRGC further consolidate

00:08:41.530 --> 00:08:46.880
its grip over Iran’s economy"
Ali Alfoneh, Arab Gulf States Institute in

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:47.880
Washington

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:52.000
For a better understanding, a big portion
of Iran’s economy is in the Revolutionary

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:53.330
Guard’s hands.

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:57.690
They own many state monopolies, including
oil companies, refineries and real estate

00:08:57.690 --> 00:08:58.690
firms.

00:08:58.690 --> 00:09:01.750
For example, 51% of Iran Telecom belongs to
them.

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:06.750
Add to this the fact they pay almost no taxes
and you have completely self-sustainable economics.

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:11.690
With a parallel army that is so well maintained,
it’s hard to have a regime change.

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:16.020
But if you thought this is the only asset
the Ayatolahs have… you are very, very mistaken…

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:22.180
You’ll see why straight ahead.

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:23.910
CHINA COMES TO THE RESCUE!

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:28.700
We said this many times in this series of
videos: China will keep buying oil from Iran.

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:31.090
They just can’t stop doing this.

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:32.860
China needs lots of dinosaur juice.

00:09:32.860 --> 00:09:35.460
And, for years, Iran has been their 6th most
important supplier.

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:40.140
We are talking about more than 800,000 barrels
that come from Iran every day.

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:42.470
With these numbers it’s hard to suddenly
change providers.

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:44.460
And yes, yes, I know what you’re thinking
now!

00:09:44.460 --> 00:09:48.950
If you’ve seen the previous videos, you
already know that America has a secret weapon

00:09:48.950 --> 00:09:52.660
to keep countries from buying Iranian oil.

00:09:52.660 --> 00:10:00.140
Basically, no oil tanker can dock in a harbour
if it’s not covered by an insurance company.

00:10:00.140 --> 00:10:04.390
And most of the insurance companies are European
or American.

00:10:04.390 --> 00:10:08.500
So… how can China keep buying oil from Iran?

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:13.120
Well… check this out…

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:21.160
Exclusive: China shifts to Iranian tankers
to keep oil flowing amid U.S. sanctions

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:22.860
Yes, you heard this right.

00:10:22.860 --> 00:10:27.880
Without insurance companies, Iran will take
care of the transport and all the risk.

00:10:27.880 --> 00:10:33.640
Do we have to care about the oil tankers maintenance?

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:34.640
Iran pays!

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:36.560
A ship can’t reach its destination?

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:37.560
Iran pays!

00:10:37.560 --> 00:10:41.920
A ship sinks in the sea?

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:42.980
Iran pays!

00:10:42.980 --> 00:10:44.970
But this is not the end of the story!

00:10:44.970 --> 00:10:48.240
Think about it… if the rest of the World
is going to stop investing in Iran… what

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:49.760
do we have left?

00:10:49.760 --> 00:10:50.760
Exactly!

00:10:50.760 --> 00:10:53.770
Freed up space for China’s money!

00:10:53.770 --> 00:10:58.670
Hence, news like this.

00:10:58.670 --> 00:11:03.610
Chinese Firm To Invest $2B In Oil Refinery
In Iran

00:11:03.610 --> 00:11:06.410
Yes, you heard that right!

00:11:06.410 --> 00:11:09.750
China is taking advantage of the void other
companies have left.

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:13.740
In fact, they are even buying the investments
other European companies made.

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:16.760
For example, TOTAL is a French oil company.

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:21.290
In 2016, they started building what was meant
to be the biggest gas field on the planet.

00:11:21.290 --> 00:11:25.270
Now, with Trump’s sanctions, chances are
they will have to retire this project.

00:11:25.270 --> 00:11:28.480
And who is ready to buy it?

00:11:28.480 --> 00:11:29.690
Exactly!

00:11:29.690 --> 00:11:30.900
China!

00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:37.420
This summer 2018, the China Development Bank
announced they will give more than 15 billion

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:41.090
dollars in loans for all kinds of projects.

00:11:41.090 --> 00:11:47.770
And you might wonder… is this big or small
Money?

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:51.480
Well… it has already helped Iran start building
5 brand new hospitals.

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:52.950
And what about other companies?

00:11:52.950 --> 00:11:56.510
Remember when I told you Iran is one of the
biggest car manufacturers in the region?

00:11:56.510 --> 00:11:59.070
Well… one of the main brands is SAIPA.

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:02.690
They have already signed a Joint venture with
another Chinese company called BRILLIANCE.

00:12:02.690 --> 00:12:04.480
But this is just the beginning!

00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:05.480
Let’s see…

00:12:05.480 --> 00:12:08.060
What is the most ambitious project in China?

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:09.060
Exactly!

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:11.300
The One Belt One Road project.

00:12:11.300 --> 00:12:14.260
That new silk road Xi Jimping wants to build.

00:12:14.260 --> 00:12:18.910
So… imagine what would be one of its biggest
hubs.

00:12:18.910 --> 00:12:22.090
China Eyes Iran as Important Belt and Road
Hub

00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:24.860
So far, they are already starting to renovate
several railroads.

00:12:24.860 --> 00:12:30.090
The idea is to connect the main Iranian cities
with high speed trains so they can transport

00:12:30.090 --> 00:12:31.090
goods.

00:12:31.090 --> 00:12:32.090
And you might wonder…

00:12:32.090 --> 00:12:33.670
Why is Iran so important?

00:12:33.670 --> 00:12:42.900
Well… just look at this map and you’ll
understand.

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:46.250
Imagine a train full of Mobile phones travelling
from China, going through Central Asia and

00:12:46.250 --> 00:12:48.150
then going from Iran to Turkey.

00:12:48.150 --> 00:12:52.270
Looks like the perfect route for China to
send their products to Europe, doesn’t it?

00:12:52.270 --> 00:12:53.970
Of course, this is just one idea.

00:12:53.970 --> 00:12:57.500
So far, Chinese businesses are already facing
many issues in Central Asia.

00:12:57.500 --> 00:13:00.870
But this is a matter for another video.

00:13:00.870 --> 00:13:04.680
The truth is China is starting to invest heavily
in Iran.

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:07.940
Does this mean Xi Jimping will save Iran’s
economy?

00:13:07.940 --> 00:13:09.000
Of course not!

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:12.490
But will this be enough for the regime to
survive?

00:13:12.490 --> 00:13:14.570
Well… maybe.

00:13:14.570 --> 00:13:18.360
And this explains why, in recent years, the
political relations between these two countries

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:25.500
are becoming more and more fluid.

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:29.410
Xi Jinping Holds Talks with President Hassan
Rouhani of Iran

00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:30.410
So now it’s your turn…

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:34.190
Do you really think Trump’s sanctions will
help end the Ayatollah regime?

